11668	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-ea5f3fca4db9e0ac8295cd73c8fac186","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:19:45.381Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The implementation scope follows the recorded narrowing of s7 to foundations.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md says “s7 is read as the foundations only” and assigns signal handling, typed tools, the tracker family, four git commands, tools.call and a report-mode scan to s7. The design covers these and leaves caller migration and deletion to s9/s10. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain this scope.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing executor lacks the proposed cancellation rechecks, and the inspected refresh tools need signal propagation.","evidence":"executeTool awaits buildApprovalRequest and the approval gate, then calls “await tool.execute(input, deps)” without checking signal.aborted. git_fetch and git_fetch_refs call runShell with timeoutMs: 120_000 and no signal; rev-parse and ls-tree call readGit, whose implementation supplies only cwd and timeoutMs. git_cat_file already supplies deps.signal to runShellBytes with a fixed 30_000 limit. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch-refs.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-tree.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed executor and per-tool changes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"queryTasks currently omits endCursor whenever hasNextPage is false.","evidence":"The design's edge-case table says this is current behaviour. queryTasks instead independently returns “hasNextPage: search.pageInfo?.hasNextPage ?? false” and “...(cursor ? { endCursor: cursor } : {})”. A nonempty final-page cursor is retained even when hasNextPage is false. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Preserve the current independent cursor behaviour, or explicitly document and test an intentional contract change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"defineGhFamily exists with the stated signature and supports runtime-checked operation families.","evidence":"op-table.ts defines defineGhFamily(spec: { id: string; description: string; ops: readonly OpDef[]; dashSafe?: boolean }): GhFamilyTool. It builds input/output schemas, registers per-op classes and limits, checks operation inputs, invokes ghExec with deps.signal, and shapes the result. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Reuse this builder; keep the documented runtime-typing exception for family tools explicit.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Exporting git definitions with the annotation ': TypedTool' preserves concrete input and output types for callTool.","evidence":"call-tool.ts defines TypedTool using “inputSchema: TSchema; ... outputSchema: TSchema”, while callTool derives its input/result through Static<T['inputSchema']> and Static<T['outputSchema']>. The design repeatedly specifies exports such as “gitFetchTool: TypedTool”. That annotation widens the schemas to TSchema, losing the concrete types the unchanged helper requires. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/rev-parse.ts]","action":"Specify inferred object definitions checked with satisfies TypedTool, or an equivalent generic type retaining each concrete schema. Require negative compile checks for invalid inputs and invalid result-field access.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The tools.call handler contract and listed change sites fully explain how transport metadata and cancellation reach ToolDeps.","evidence":"ToolDeps requires a numeric requestId and send callback. RpcHandler receives only params and TrustedRpcContext; that context exposes connectionIdentity and lifecycle signals, but no wire request id or send callback. The stream handler receives send and signal separately. The design promises all these values plus client cancellation without selecting a unary/stream protocol or documenting the required transport adaptation. Its inventory omits server.ts, request-context.ts and the shared IPC client/types. It also promises both an IPC error and a failed ToolResult for an unknown tool in different sections. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/request-context.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/shared/ipc-client.ts, src/shared/types.ts]","action":"Define the exact wire protocol and metadata adapter, cancellation mechanism, and one unknown-tool response. Include all necessary transport/type change sites. Document request-to-connection ownership and approval subscription relationships in prose or a small sequence diagram; no ERD is necessary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed tracker family has sufficiently concrete contracts for later Stories to consume.","evidence":"The design lists operation descriptions but supplies no family id, operation identifiers, exact per-op input/output shapes or endpoint templates. These are required by OpDef, which includes name, command, cls, limitS, fields, args and out. Existing wrappers have materially different contracts: ghCreateIssue returns a ref string, ghCreateIssueTyped returns {ref,id,typed}, and queryTasks returns {tasks,pageInfo,total?}, whereas defineGhFamily adds an op discriminator. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Provide a per-operation contract table with stable identifiers, required/optional fields, output schemas, fixed endpoint/argv templates and wrapper-to-tool mapping. State which wrapper-level transformations remain for s10.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding optional timeoutMs to git_cat_file can preserve existing callers without rewriting stored records.","evidence":"git_cat_file currently has no timeoutMs input and passes timeoutMs: 30_000 directly to runShellBytes. Its data is constructed per invocation as existence/type/size/object results. Keeping the same default and output schema while adding an optional bounded input requires no stored-record migration. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/schemas.ts]","action":"Preserve the existing default, output schema and failure messages; test omitted timeoutMs against the existing behaviour.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Building the tracker family and four git commands in s7, while postponing caller migration, respects the recorded Story ownership decisions.","evidence":"The 2026-10-26 decision log explicitly assigns the tracker family and config, ls-remote, update-ref and rm to s7, without adding s8 as a dependency. The subsequent split assigns site migration to s9/s10 and deletion/failing scan mode to s10. The design follows these decisions. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain the ownership notes and avoid moving production callers during s7.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Passing deps.signal to the existing runShell helper is sufficient to ensure no command starts after cancellation.","evidence":"runShell spawns the child first and then installs an abort listener: “const child = spawn(command!, args, ...)” precedes “options.signal?.addEventListener('abort', onAbort, { once: true })”. It never checks an already-aborted signal. Unlike runShellBytes, passing an already-aborted signal can therefore start a process that runs until its fixed timeout. This matters after awaited git_show commands and any approval/preview work; one executor check does not protect subsequent subprocess launches. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/show.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Specify an aborted-signal check immediately before every subprocess launch, in the selected tools or helper, and stop subsequent commands after cancellation. Test already-aborted helper input and cancellation between git_show commands, in addition to cancellation of a running process.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The acceptance mapping uses the effective s7 acceptance criteria.","evidence":"The decision log defines five effective criteria: ac1 hooks, ac2 destructive denial, ac3 cancellation/timeouts, ac4 typed family/four git tools, and ac5 validated caller/report scan. The design maps six old criterion ids instead: for example its ac1 covers typed calls, ac4 covers hooks, and ac6 covers migration inventory. Although many relevant test subjects are listed, the claimed criterion mapping is incorrect. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Rewrite the mapping against the five effective criteria, explicitly covering callTool with caller workflow as well as tools.call. Keep s9/s10 obligations separately identified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The normal tsc build will execute the proposed compile-time checks placed under __tests__.","evidence":"The design places typed-git-tools.test.ts under src/daemon/tools/__tests__ and calls for a compile-time check run with tsc. tsconfig.json explicitly excludes “**/__tests__/**” and “**/*.test.ts”; package.json's build invokes that configuration. Running these tests through tsx does not supply TypeScript type checking. [files: tsconfig.json, package.json]","action":"Specify a dedicated noEmit type-check configuration or compiler harness that includes the type fixtures, and wire its command into the required checks. Include assertions that reject invalid inputs and verify concrete output types.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":5,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T14:19:45.381Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
433	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"d6c2cde5143d4f42ab611c2dfdc4b7a2","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:23:27.275Z","operation":"review","revision":{"number":3,"contentHash":"633cd49799b27b3a0fcf5d07b65491777e74010fd7e220dfd73d5c3c380e348a"},"outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"reviewed by the daemon: block","data":{"counts":{"high":2,"med":5,"low":5}}}}}
11287	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-7788b5b412ff760a45223d94a2c44c2d","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:31:01.848Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The refresh-tool foundations cover effective ac3, including carrying remaining time.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md requires the refresh tools to carry 'deps.signal and the remaining time'. policy-refresh.ts passes deadline.remainingMs() to local commands; git-async.ts uses 'timeout: left'. The design specifies fixed tool timeouts and adds a lowerable timeout only to git_cat_file, without specifying how the other tools accept remaining time or receive a deadline-derived signal. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/workflow/team/policy-refresh.ts, src/workflow/team/git-async.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch-refs.ts]","action":"Specify a complete remaining-budget mechanism for every refresh tool, including new git_ls_remote, while preserving the fixed limits as ceilings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor and text shell helper currently lack the proposed pre-execution abort checks.","evidence":"executeTool awaits buildApprovalRequest and the gate, then calls 'await tool.execute(input, deps)' without checking signal.aborted. runShell calls spawn before adding its abort listener. runShellBytes explicitly returns early for 'options.signal?.aborted'. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Preserve the stated distinction between the two shell helpers when implementing cancellation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"queryTasks currently preserves a nonempty endCursor independently of hasNextPage.","evidence":"queryTasks sets 'hasNextPage: search.pageInfo?.hasNextPage ?? false' and independently spreads '...(cursor ? { endCursor: cursor } : {})'; total is included only when issueCount is a number. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Retain these independently computed fields in the new operation and later wrapper migration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"callTool and defineGhFamily exist with the reusable contracts described.","evidence":"call-tool.ts declares the stated generic callTool signature over TypedTool. op-table.ts exports defineGhFamily with id, description, ops and optional dashSafe; its custom output builder supports deterministic transformations and it registers per-operation approval classes and limits. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Use custom output builders for tracker response transformations and retain the family's runtime checking.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"tools.call can obtain sessionId from the existing trusted connection context while leaving that context unchanged.","evidence":"TrustedRpcContext contains connectionIdentity, daemonEpoch, connectionExecution, connectionSession and lifecycle metadata; it has no sessionId. TrustedConnectionSession also has no sessionId. ToolDeps requires 'sessionId: string'. The design supplies no valid source or mapping for this required field. [files: src/daemon/request-context.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"Define how a tool session is established or resolved from trusted metadata, including connection-only callers; update the context contract and change inventory if necessary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The change-site inventory is sufficient to make gh_tracker available through the registry.","evidence":"registerGhTools in gh/index.ts explicitly imports and registers each tool and family using registerTool. defineGhFamily registers approval and timeout metadata, but does not register the tool itself. The proposed gh change sites omit gh/index.ts and never specify adding gh_tracker to registerGhTools. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/registry.ts]","action":"Add the tracker import and registration to registerGhTools and test lookup and execution through the registry.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed type fixtures remain outside the normal emitting build.","evidence":"tsconfig.json includes 'src/**/*.ts' and excludes only '**/__tests__/**' and '**/*.test.ts'. The proposed '__type-tests__/git-tools.typecheck.ts' matches neither exclusion, so normal tsc will also compile and emit it despite the dedicated noEmit configuration. [files: tsconfig.json, package.json]","action":"Explicitly exclude __type-tests__ from the root configuration and explicitly include them, with the appropriate exclude override, in the dedicated configuration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed shell and git_cat_file changes can preserve existing caller shapes without a stored-data migration.","evidence":"ShellResult is a process-result interface, readGit currently takes four arguments, and git_cat_file currently uses a fixed 30000 ms timeout. Adding an optional result field, optional final parameter and optional timeout input with the existing default requires no persistent record rewrite. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts]","action":"Keep the default timeout and existing result fields unchanged, and test calls that omit the additions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The narrowed foundation scope and ownership of later call-site migrations agree with the recorded split.","evidence":"tool-registry.md assigns foundation work to s7, explicitly assigns the four git commands and tracker family to it, and moves call-site replacement and wrapper deletion to s9/s10. S009/EXT.md and S010/EXT.md confirm those migration responsibilities. The design's stream/approval prose states one call per stream, cancellation ownership and a daemon-wide approval broker; this adequately documents the relevant runtime relationships without requiring an ERD. No generated companion is linked for visual verification. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/EXT.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S010/EXT.md, src/daemon/approval.ts, src/daemon/approval-broker.ts]","action":"Keep production call-site migration and production hook registration outside s7; retain the relationship and compatibility prose.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Reusing the existing gh family failure path preserves typed-issue rejection text in failure.original as promised.","evidence":"ghFailureOf computes 'const original = probeText.length > 0 ? probeText : undefined' and returns ordinary rejected failures with original only when that probe text exists. A plain HTTP 422 issue-type rejection therefore retains API text in message, but not failure.original. defineGhFamily forwards this failure before calling any custom output builder. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Explicitly design preservation of the API diagnostic for tracker failures, including the helper change site or a supported family seam, and test the exact failure.original consumed by the fallback.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing approval broker supports subscription-independent call ownership and cancellation of pending approvals.","evidence":"ApprovalBroker stores pending requests separately from subscriber streams, broadcasts requests to subscribers, resolves no-client when none exist, attaches the call's abort signal, and settles cancellation through finish. approval.subscribe and approval.answer expose these operations separately. [files: src/daemon/approval-broker.ts, src/daemon/approval.ts]","action":"Exercise this existing broker through tools.call rather than introducing another pending-approval holder.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The acceptance mapping fully tests effective ac3's remaining-time requirement.","evidence":"The upstream ac3 explicitly includes 'remaining time'. The proposed tests cover abort propagation and git_cat_file's lowerable timeout, but none verifies that successive refresh operations receive the diminishing shared budget or that a running non-cat-file command stops at that budget. Existing git-async.ts explicitly enforces 'timeout: left'. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/workflow/team/git-async.ts, src/workflow/team/policy-refresh.ts]","action":"Add a recorded-executor or controlled-clock test proving diminishing budgets across multiple operations and termination at the shared deadline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The tasks_query test expectations agree with the proposed output semantics.","evidence":"The contract and edge-case prose require hasNextPage=false when pageInfo is absent, matching queryTasks' '?? false'. The test strategy instead says the operation 'returns no pageInfo fields when the API gives none', which would exclude the required default field. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Specify one consistent assertion: pageInfo contains hasNextPage:false and omits endCursor when the API supplies no pageInfo.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":4,"med":3,"low":6,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T14:31:01.848Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
