9381	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-5a19598e452fe1acca72b970822d4578","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:40:16.269Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s7 implements foundations while s9 and s10 own migration and removal.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly records 's7 is read as the foundations only' and lists the five effective criteria. It transfers site migration, deletion and artifact-equivalence checks to s9/s10. The proposed scope follows that recorded decision. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Use the recorded five criteria as the implementation baseline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor and runShell currently lack the proposed pre-start cancellation checks.","evidence":"executeTool builds the approval request, awaits gate().ask(request, deps.signal), then invokes tool.execute without an aborted check. runShell calls spawn before installing its abort listener. runShellBytes already returns early for options.signal?.aborted. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed checks and record aborted state for cancellation during runShell execution.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The executor truncates failure.original on any tool failure.","evidence":"The executor's failed() helper slices original to ORIGINAL_MAX_CHARS, but executeTool returns tool failures unchanged: 'if (!result.success) return result;'. Thus a gh_tracker failure.original supplied by ghFailureOf will not be truncated by the executor as §3.4 claims. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Specify an explicit cap in the new diagnostic path, or correct the claim and deliberately document uncapped diagnostics. Preserve existing gh failure objects.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"callTool and defineGhFamily provide the stated reusable foundations.","evidence":"callTool has the stated generic signature and derives input/output through Static<T[...Schema]>. TypedTool requires both TypeBox schemas. defineGhFamily builds a GhFamilyTool from OpDef entries, with per-op approval, limits, validation and output shaping. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Reuse these contracts without widening the exported git definitions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing project item-add tool can replace ghAddProjectItem.","evidence":"ghAddProjectItem executes project item-add with project number, owner and issue URL and returns a boolean based on command success. gh:project:item-add accepts number, owner and url, executes the same command, and returns success with {number, url}; the wrapper reads no missing API identifier. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/project.ts]","action":"Resolve the design's open mapping question in favor of the existing tool; retain the planned regression test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The four new git tools have sufficiently specified contracts for downstream callers.","evidence":"§3.5 names purposes and destructive classes but supplies no concrete input/output shapes or timeout values. Existing callers require distinct ls-remote forms: branch-resolution.ts uses '--symref remote HEAD' and '--heads remote refs/heads/<name>'; handoff.ts uses path-specific rm and deletion of named refs. The design refers to 'the new tools’ limits' without defining them. [files: src/workflow/team/branch-resolution.ts, src/workflow/team/handoff.ts, src/understanding/identity.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Add a per-tool contract table defining fields, defaults, output shapes, argv, limits and invalid-input handling, including ls-remote patterns, config missing-key behavior, rm paths and update-ref deletion targets.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing generic stream transport supports the proposed tools.call handler without changing server or trusted-context signatures.","evidence":"StreamHandler receives (params, send, signal, context), while RpcHandler lacks send. directDispatch combines request and connection lifetime signals and aborts on cancellation. TrustedRpcContext contains connectionIdentity and optional connectionExecution, with no sessionId. handler-runtime already registers approval.subscribe in streamHandlers. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/request-context.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts]","action":"Add the handler and method-class entry as proposed. The ownership prose adequately describes the stream-to-call and subscriber-to-approval relationships; no additional ERD is necessary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed foundation changes can remain additive without rewriting stored records.","evidence":"ShellResult currently has no aborted field; ShellOptions already has optional signal. readGit currently takes four arguments, allowing an optional fifth parameter without changing callers. git_cat_file uses a fixed 30000 ms timeout and an input schema to which the optional bounded field can be added. These are runtime contracts, not persistent record changes. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts]","action":"Keep new fields optional and retain the existing default timeout and failure compatibility tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Building the tracker family and four git commands in s7 respects the recorded Story boundaries.","evidence":"The plan records explicit user decisions that s7 builds the tracker family and config, ls-remote, update-ref and rm, without adding s8 to dependsOn. It also states that s7 registers no production hook and that later Stories move callers. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/coverage.ts]","action":"Retain the proposed coverage-table ownership notes and handoffs.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Cancellation and approval failures can use the existing failure and transport contracts.","evidence":"The executor already defines cancelled, timed-out and no-client approval denials and returns unknown tools as rejected ToolResults. approval.subscribe registers a daemon-broker subscriber independently of the tool stream. directDispatch suppresses frames after cancellation, so a disconnected caller need not receive a terminal response. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/approval.ts, src/daemon/approval-broker.ts, src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed pre-execute checks and test cancellation through the transport and broker together.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The effective s7 criteria have planned tests, including a separate compile-time check.","evidence":"The five criteria recorded in tool-registry.md map to the design's hook, denial, deadline, typed-tool/registration and IPC/scan tests. tsconfig.json includes src/**/*.ts and src/**/*.tsx while excluding __tests__ and *.test.ts; package.json currently builds with tsc and check-model-definitions.mjs, supporting the proposed separate noEmit fixture configuration and additional build checks. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, tsconfig.json, package.json]","action":"Retain the mapping and make the new git contract tests assert the explicit shapes and limits requested under change-sites. This assesses the test plan, not execution of tests that have yet to be implemented.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T14:40:16.269Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
