10975	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-1cdf3def7bbac2aa7b4203f6d723107d","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:13:08.282Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The foundation-only scope covers the five effective s7 criteria and leaves caller migration and enforcement to s9/s10.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md states 's7 is read as the foundations only' and lists hooks, destructive denial, cancellation, typed tools, tools.call and the report-mode scan. It explicitly assigns site moves and deletion to s9/s10. The design covers these responsibilities. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Use this recorded amendment as the acceptance baseline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor currently validates input before approval, lacks the proposed cancellation rechecks, and returns tool-built failures unchanged.","evidence":"executeTool calls validateAgainstSchema before buildApprovalRequest, passes deps.signal to gate().ask, then calls tool.execute without an aborted check. Its result handling contains 'if (!result.success) return result;'. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Preserve this ordering and unchanged-failure behavior while adding cancellation checks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runShell currently kills only its child, whereas runShellBytes checks pre-abort and kills a detached process group.","evidence":"runShell uses 'const onAbort = () => child.kill('SIGKILL')' and resolves on error/close without an entry abort check. runShellBytes checks options.signal?.aborted, spawns with 'detached: process.platform !== 'win32'', and calls process.kill(-child.pid, 'SIGKILL'). [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Proceed with the proposed shared kill helper.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"defineGhFamily can implement the proposed parameterized fixed API endpoints through its existing op-table contract, with only the diagnostic field added.","evidence":"OpDef.command is 'readonly string[]'. Arg supports input positionals, flags, spreads and fixed literal tokens. buildArgv starts with \"['gh', ...def.command]\" and never interpolates endpoint templates or constructs 'title=value' arguments. Consequently repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}, query-string encoding and repeated labels[]=value cannot be expressed as designed using the stated contract. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Specify a bounded, internal argv-builder extension with endpoint encoding and field construction, enumerate its change sites, and test it. Do not expose a raw endpoint input.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Checking registered.outputSchema identity is an authorized refinement compatible with registration wrappers.","evidence":"callTool currently dispatches solely by tool.id and casts result.data. registerTool overwrites existing ids. Both withFailureNet and withGhFailureNet spread the definition, retaining schema references. The plan explicitly permits 'same object or same outputSchema'. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Implement the proposed check and wrapper/overwrite regression tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing stream transport, trusted context and session routing support the proposed tools.call handler without redesigning the server.","evidence":"StreamHandler receives params, send, signal and optional TrustedRpcContext. directDispatch combines cancellation signals and aborts on cancellation; the socket-close path cancels in-flight work. TrustedRpcContext contains connectionIdentity and connectionExecution but no sessionId. daemon/index.ts routes indexing/admin to workers and explicitly keeps session methods local. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/request-context.ts, src/daemon/threads/router.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts]","action":"Retain the generic stream path and test tools.call through the real dispatch/socket cancellation path.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The git index already exports every definition needed by the proposed fixture and future typed callers.","evidence":"src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts imports 34 definitions and exports registerGitTools, but contains no definition re-exports. The design repeatedly describes the fixture as listing every git tool 'exported from' this index without specifying those new exports. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts]","action":"Explicitly add definition re-exports to the index contract, or specify direct module imports for the fixture and consumers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed SAFE_REF and SAFE_PATH restrictions preserve the real callers' accepted inputs.","evidence":"isSafeRefName explicitly accepts 'any script, '+', '#', ...' and its implementation permits these characters. branch-resolution.ts accepts supplied branches through that predicate. The proposed ASCII-only SAFE_REF rejects such existing valid branches/remotes. assertSafeArg also explicitly permits paths starting with '-' after '--', whereas proposed git_rm rejects them even though handoff.ts places paths after '--'. [files: src/workflow/team/sighting-store.ts, src/workflow/team/branch-resolution.ts, src/workflow/team/handoff.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Derive schemas from the callers' existing safety rules, including Unicode and valid punctuation; allow leading-dash paths after '--'. Add compatibility cases for these inputs or obtain an explicit behavior-change decision.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The added foundations respect recorded Story ownership and document the new interaction relationships adequately.","evidence":"The plan assigns the four git commands and tracker family to s7, exempts indexer/self-update, and delegates caller moves to s9/s10. The design documents client-to-stream-to-executor direction, one owning stream per call, daemon-wide approval subscriptions, trusted-context authority and registration-wrapper ownership. These prose contracts adequately describe the relevant relationships; an ERD or UX mock is unnecessary for this foundation change. No generated companion is claimed or linked for visual verification. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/approval.ts, src/daemon/request-context.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Preserve these boundaries; document the additional op-table extension required by this review.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"All refresh tools receive the promised bounded settlement after their deadline, including git_cat_file.","evidence":"gitCatFileTool executes runShellBytes. That helper only invokes finish from child 'error' and 'close' events; its kill callback has no settlement timer. The design adds the 2-second fallback specifically to runShell while saying runShellBytes behavior is unchanged. Sharing its kill helper does not give the byte runner a settlement bound, so the stated refresh-wide bound remains unsupported for git_cat_file. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts]","action":"Specify bounded settlement and stream cleanup for runShellBytes too, and test git_cat_file through that path, or explicitly narrow the deadline guarantee.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The opt-in gh diagnostic seam fits existing failure propagation without changing other tools' failure objects.","evidence":"ghFailureOf currently puts stderr into original for spawn errors and otherwise derives original only from probe output. defineGhFamily forwards failures before output shaping; executeTool returns failed results unchanged. Applying a cap in the opt-in command-exit seam therefore addresses the actual propagation path. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Keep spawn-error handling and non-opted-in failures unchanged as specified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each effective acceptance criterion has a concrete planned proving test.","evidence":"The plan's five effective criteria correspond to the design's workflow-hook tests, destructive denial tests, executor/shell/deadline tests, typed-tool and tracker-family tests, and handler/scan tests. tsconfig.json currently excludes __tests__ and *.test.ts while including src/**/*.ts and src/**/*.tsx, supporting the separate typecheck configuration and explicit fixture exclusion. This assesses the proposed mapping, not execution of tests that have yet to be built. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, tsconfig.json, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Extend the existing mapped suites to cover the argv-builder, compatibility and byte-runner settlement findings above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":3,"med":1,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T15:13:08.282Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
