11115	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-46c790e06c0e5e0c4bb255c0d1028ec4","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:25:42.608Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the five effective s7 foundation criteria and leaves call-site migration to s9 and s10.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly says “s7 is read as the foundations only” and lists hooks, destructive-call denial, abort propagation, typed tools, tools.call and the report-mode scan. It assigns the former migration and deletion criteria to s9 and s10. The proposed work follows that split. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain the effective-criteria reference and the explicit handover.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor currently validates schematized input before approval, returns tool failures unchanged, and lacks the proposed abort rechecks.","evidence":"executeTool calls validateAgainstSchema before resolveApprovalClass/buildApprovalRequest, passes deps.signal to gate().ask, then calls tool.execute without an aborted check. Its result path contains “if (!result.success) return result;”. Only failed() slices original to ORIGINAL_MAX_CHARS. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Implement the two cancellation checks while preserving this ordering and failure passthrough.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shell helpers have the cancellation and settlement weaknesses described in the design.","evidence":"runShell has no pre-spawn aborted check or detached option; its abort callback is “() => child.kill('SIGKILL')”. runShellBytes checks options.signal?.aborted, spawns detached on non-win32, and uses process.kill(-child.pid, 'SIGKILL'). Its kill paths do not settle directly; finish is invoked from error and close handlers. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Retain the shared bounded-settlement implementation and real descendant-process tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"defineGhFamily is an existing reusable foundation that builds and wraps a tool without registering that tool in the registry.","evidence":"defineGhFamily constructs input/output schemas, approval handling, argv execution and output shaping, then returns “withGhFailureNet(tool as unknown as GhFamilyTool)”. It registers approval and limit metadata, but does not call registerTool. Its custom output builder receives stdout, stderr, input, deps and truncated. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Reuse this foundation and explicitly register gh_tracker as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The specified op-table changes are sufficient to express the promised owner/repo schema patterns.","evidence":"FieldSpec currently exposes kind, values, minimum, description and empty; it has no pattern or schema override. fieldSchema's string branch returns “Type.String({ ...(spec.empty === true ? {} : { minLength: 1 }), ...d })”. Adding only Arg variants and diagnostic cannot produce the promised owner/repo pattern in the input schema. A refuseInput check would occur inside execute, after approval. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Specify an additive FieldSpec pattern/schema facility, its propagation through fieldSchema and shared-field comparison, and tests proving invalid names are rejected before approval.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed qs variant completely specifies how tracker listing arguments are constructed.","evidence":"The proposed qs entries contain only key, field and optional. comments_list requires the fixed query per_page=100, while issue listings also require state=all; these are absent from their declared inputs. Existing buildArgv reads values directly from input and supplies no normalization/default stage. The design also requires labels to be joined by commas without specifying that transformation in qs. The current wrapper explicitly constructs “state=all&per_page=100&labels=${labels.map(encodeURIComponent).join(',')}”. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Define fixed query values and list serialization in the argument contract, or explicitly define the normalization stage supplying them. Include exact-argv fixtures for constants, labels and optional since.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The lowerable git_cat_file timeout can be added without migrating stored data or changing the default read limit.","evidence":"gitCatFileTool currently declares no timeoutMs input and calls runShellBytes with “timeoutMs: 30_000”. Its result is constructed from the command response rather than a persisted timeout field. Adding an optional bounded input with the same default preserves existing callers' limit and requires no stored-record rewrite. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts]","action":"Keep the timeout optional and preserve the existing output and diagnostic branches.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Building the tracker family and four additional git commands in s7 is authorized rather than an accidental redesign of s8 or s10.","evidence":"The plan's 2026-10-26 decisions explicitly assign the narrow tracker family and config, ls-remote, update-ref and rm to s7, and say s8 is not added to dependsOn. The later split retains these foundations in s7 while assigning migrations to s9/s10. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Keep coverage-table ownership notes aligned with these decisions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The tools.call relationship and lifecycle changes are adequately documented in prose without requiring a separate diagram.","evidence":"The design identifies the calling stream as owner of cancellation, the daemon broker as owner of pending approvals, and approval.subscribe/approval.answer as the separate approval endpoints. This matches StreamHandler's signal/context parameters, directDispatch's combined abort signal, and ApprovalBroker's broadcast to subscribed streams. These descriptions resolve direction, ownership and multiplicity; no generated companion is claimed. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/request-context.ts, src/daemon/approval.ts, src/daemon/approval-broker.ts]","action":"Retain this ownership description. A sequence diagram would be optional.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Comparing only outputSchema reference identity rejects every replacement definition registered under the same id.","evidence":"registerTool unconditionally executes “byId.set(tool.id, tool)”. Both failure wrappers spread the supplied definition. Consequently, registering {...original, execute: differentExecute} preserves original.outputSchema and passes the proposed check, although a different implementation runs. A replacement can also change inputSchema or approval while retaining the output schema. The check protects output-schema identity, not the definition identity promised by §§2.7, 3.3 and the error paths. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Define and preserve explicit definition provenance through supported wrappers, then check it in callTool. Test same-output-schema replacements with changed execute, inputSchema and approval. Alternatively, narrow the stated guarantee if schema identity alone is intended.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing approval broker supports the proposed disconnected-client and pending-cancellation handling.","evidence":"ApprovalBroker.ask returns no-client when no stream is subscribed, registers an abort listener that finishes with cancelled, and times out pending requests. unsubscribe resolves all pending requests as no-client when the last subscriber leaves. approval.subscribe holds its subscription until its stream signal aborts. [files: src/daemon/approval-broker.ts, src/daemon/approval.ts, src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"Reuse these paths and verify them through tools.call integration tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each effective s7 acceptance criterion has a concrete proposed proving test.","evidence":"Against the five effective criteria in tool-registry.md, §6 maps ac1 to workflow hooks, ac2 to approval denial, ac3 to abort/deadline and timeout tests, ac4 to typing/tool-family contracts, and ac5 to handler validation and scan fixtures. Existing call-tool.test.ts demonstrates the registry/fake-definition fixture style, and tsconfig.json currently excludes __tests__ and *.test.ts, supporting a separate typecheck configuration. This verifies test planning, not execution of future tests. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/call-tool.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts, tsconfig.json]","action":"Add regression cases for the contract gaps above, particularly replacements sharing outputSchema. Do not describe list membership as a compile-time completeness guarantee: an omitted definition is caught by the proposed filesystem inventory test, not by satisfies on the list.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":2,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T15:25:42.608Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
