10271	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-f6a137dfbc28f7af2eef37835a6a83c2","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:06:30.871Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the five effective foundation criteria and leaves call-site migration to s9 and s10.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly says 's7 is read as the foundations only' and assigns site moves, deletion and failing enforcement to s9/s10. The design supplies hooks integration, approvals, cancellation foundations, typed tools, tools.call and the reporting scan. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain the explicit reference to the superseding plan decision.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor currently validates input before approval, returns tool-authored failures unchanged, and lacks the proposed pre-execution abort checks.","evidence":"executeTool validates input before buildApprovalRequest, passes deps.signal to gate().ask, then calls tool.execute without checking signal.aborted. Its result path contains 'if (!result.success) return result;'. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Implement the two proposed abort checks while preserving pipeline order.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runShell lacks pre-abort and process-group handling, while runShellBytes already has both but lacks bounded settlement after killing.","evidence":"runShell spawns without detached and its abort callback calls child.kill('SIGKILL'). runShellBytes checks options.signal?.aborted and uses process.kill(-child.pid, 'SIGKILL'); its finish function is invoked only by error/close handlers. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Proceed with the shared bounded-settlement helper.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"gh_project_manage create supplies the structured fields needed by ghCreateProject.","evidence":"ghCreateProject reads JSON 'number' and 'url' and returns null without a numeric number. The existing create op declares out: { kind: 'mutation' }; shape() produces only { op, ok: true, target, message }. Thus project creation is already a confirmed mapping mismatch, beyond the design's singled-out uncertainty about item-add. The fallback instruction anticipates adding an op but leaves its actual contract unspecified. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/manage.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Specify the additional project-create tracker op now, including input, structured number/url output, approval and timeout. Update the operation inventory and mapping tests accordingly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The listed signal changes suffice for tools.call to kill a running tool's process tree on disconnect.","evidence":"tools.call accepts any registered tool, but gitDiffTool.execute accepts only input and starts both shell calls without signal. ghIssueListTool.execute likewise accepts only input and invokes ghExec without signal. These implementations are unchanged by the proposed refresh-only signal edits. Additionally, ghExec's ambiguous-error auth probe calls runShellBytes with timeoutMs: 10000 and no signal, even when the original operation received one. Aborting the stream therefore cannot deliver the promised cancellation throughout these execution paths. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/issue.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Inventory and propagate cancellation through every subprocess path exposed by tools.call, including legacy exports, secondary commands and auth probes; alternatively explicitly constrain the method's supported tools and cancellation contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The generic stream transport supports the proposed handler shape and socket-owned cancellation without changing TrustedRpcContext.","evidence":"StreamHandler receives params, send, signal and optional context. TrustedRpcContext has connectionIdentity and connectionExecution, without sessionId. IpcServer tracks cancellation per request and invokes lifetime.abort()/cancel() on connection loss; terminal frames are identified by stream 'done'/'error'. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/request-context.ts, src/shared/types.ts]","action":"Use the existing {id, stream, data} frame envelope and keep execution metadata sourced from trusted context.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed additions require no persistent-record migration and can preserve existing tool schemas.","evidence":"The examined changes concern transient shell results, tool definitions and IPC arguments. Existing git_cat_file has additionalProperties:false and no timeoutMs, so adding an optional bounded field is compatible with existing requests. FieldSpec and Arg currently lack the proposed additions; existing specs can retain their current schema construction. ApprovalBroker explicitly keeps pending state only in memory. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/approval-broker.ts]","action":"Preserve omission behavior and existing field semantics in regression fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The scope amendments and relationship documentation adequately distinguish s7 foundations from adjacent ownership.","evidence":"The plan expressly assigns the tracker family and four git commands to s7 and moves callers to s9/s10. Existing git registration wraps definitions, while gh exports are already wrapped; the proposed prose defines copy-to-immediate-original ownership, registry relationships, bounded traversal and compatibility. It also describes stream ownership separately from daemon-wide approval subscriptions. These relationships are sufficiently explicit without an ERD; no generated visual companion is claimed or linked in the supplied design. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/approval.ts]","action":"Keep shared public signatures unchanged and preserve the documented migration boundaries.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The opt-in diagnostic seam correctly accounts for executor failure handling and preserves existing gh failure behavior.","evidence":"ghFailureOf's spawn-error branch sets original to trimmed stderr; ordinary exit failures derive original from probe output. executeTool returns a tool's failed result unchanged, so its private failed() cap cannot cap the new diagnostic. Applying the cap within the opt-in gh seam is therefore necessary and correctly placed. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Preserve branch precedence and verify opt-out failure objects remain unchanged.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"All five effective acceptance criteria have explicit proposed test mappings grounded in available seams.","evidence":"The design maps ac1–ac5 to hook, approval, deadline, typing/inventory, handler and scan tests. The executor exposes _setApprovalGateForTests and _setCommonApprovalForTests, and shell-helper exposes timeout scaling. The separate typecheck configuration addresses the root tsconfig's exclusion of __tests__ and *.test.ts. These are proposed tests, not verified passing implementations. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, tsconfig.json, package.json]","action":"Retain the independent inventory test and negative compile fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The tests cover the promised cancellation of already-running tools through tools.call.","evidence":"The proposed call-handler tests cover stream abort and pending approval cancellation, while subprocess cancellation tests exercise shell helpers and selected refresh tools. They do not exercise an already-running legacy gh tool or git_diff through the real stream path, nor cancellation during ghExec's auth probe. The inspected implementations omit signal forwarding on those paths. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/issue.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"Add stream-disconnect integration cases for running legacy git/gh tools and an in-progress auth probe, asserting subprocess termination and bounded settlement.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":2,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T16:06:30.871Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
