11832	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-ff24725dc70aa692619f4133682670d0","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:21:42.595Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The foundations-only scope and deferral of call-site migration match the recorded upstream decisions.","evidence":"The plan explicitly states 's7 is read as the foundations only' and lists five effective criteria. S009 owns workflow/daemon migration and the refresh sending side; S010 owns tracker/client migration, wrapper deletion and failing scan mode. The LLD preserves that division. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/EXT.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S010/EXT.md]","action":"Retain this scope and the explicit handovers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor and shell helpers currently have the cancellation gaps described by the design.","evidence":"executeTool calls 'await tool.execute(input, deps)' without a signal recheck or ambient context and returns 'if (!result.success) return result'. runShell installs an abort listener that only calls child.kill('SIGKILL'), without an entry abort check or detached process group. runShellBytes checks an already-aborted signal and kills the process group, but its kill paths do not independently settle the promise. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Preserve the existing failure-return behavior while implementing cancellation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The provenance proposal accounts for the actual difference between git and gh registration.","evidence":"Git registration uses 'register(withFailureNet(gitDiffTool))' and equivalent calls; withFailureNet returns a spread copy. ghProjectListTool is exported as 'withGhFailureNet({...})', and defineGhFamily likewise returns its wrapped object. callTool currently executes by id and casts result.data without checking definition identity. These are the distinct cases the proposed identity-or-provenance walk handles. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/project.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Keep identity acceptance for exported gh objects and wrapper-chain acceptance for git definitions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed op-table extensions and project_create result address capabilities absent from the reused abstractions.","evidence":"FieldSpec has no pattern, and Arg contains only pos, spread, last, flag and lit. buildInputSchema compares shared field specs using JSON.stringify after removing description and values. Mutation outputs contain only '{op, ok, target, message}', whereas ghCreateProject reads a numeric number and url. gh_project_list already returns raw project rows, and its schema includes number, title, url and closed. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/project.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/schemas.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Keep the extensions additive and preserve the existing project-list mapping.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Changing only the shared shell helpers makes every registered tool subprocess cancellable with process-tree termination and bounded settlement.","evidence":"Registered tools bypass those helpers. shellExecDetachedTool directly calls 'spawn(cmd!, args, { cwd, env, stdio: ... , shell: false })', handles abort with 'child.kill(\"SIGKILL\")', and settles on error/close. Its process is not actually detached into another group. awsLogsTailTool's follow branch similarly spawns directly and aborts with SIGTERM. Neither reads the proposed ambient signal or uses the shared settlement helper. registerShellTools registers shellExecDetachedTool, and registerBuiltinTools includes shell and cloud tools. Thus tools.call's guarantee for EVERY registered tool is false as written. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/shell/exec-detached.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/shell/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/cloud/aws/logs.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Inventory direct subprocess implementations inside the tool registry and route them through a shared cancellable streaming/process lifecycle, preserving progress output. Include all required change sites, or explicitly revise the universal contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The lowerable git_cat_file timeout can be added without changing existing persisted records or the existing default read contract.","evidence":"gitCatFileTool currently has no timeoutMs input, invokes runShellBytes with 'timeoutMs: 30_000', and already forwards deps.signal. Its output is built from the existing GitCatFileDataSchema and object framing logic. An optional bounded timeout with the same default requires no stored-record migration and need not alter those outputs. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/schemas.ts]","action":"Retain the 30000 ms default, existing framing/limit failures and output schema.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Building the tracker family and four additional git commands in s7 is an authorized boundary adjustment.","evidence":"The plan records the user's decisions that 's7 builds the narrow typed tracker family' and 's7 builds config, ls-remote, update-ref and rm', with coverage-table amendments and no added s8 dependency. The LLD follows these decisions while leaving caller migration to s9/s10. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/EXT.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S010/EXT.md]","action":"Carry the amendments into the coverage tables as specified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed relationships are documented sufficiently in prose without requiring an ERD or UX companion.","evidence":"The LLD specifies wrapper-copy → immediate-original links, their WeakMap ownership and bounded traversal; stream → call ownership; and daemon-broker → multiple approval subscribers with answers on approval.answer. These correspond to the actual registry, stream-handler and broker boundaries. No persisted entity relationship or UI layout is introduced, and no generated companion is claimed or linked for this design. [files: src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/approval.ts, src/daemon/approval-broker.ts]","action":"No mandatory visual addition is needed; update the signal-lifetime prose when correcting the cancellation findings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Wrapping only tool.execute cancels all subprocesses associated with a tool call, including cancellation during approval-preview construction.","evidence":"buildApprovalRequest awaits 'tool.buildApprovalGate(input)' before execution. gitPushTool's async preview calls readBranch when ref is absent; gitResetTool's preview calls currentBranch and willNeedForcePush. These helpers start runShell commands without a signal. The LLD explicitly wraps ONLY tool.execute, so these preview subprocesses have no ambient call signal. A disconnect during preview cannot kill them; the later executor recheck only prevents the mutation from starting. [files: src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/reset.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Design cancellation for asynchronous preview work as well as execute, while preserving pipeline order and keeping hooks outside the execution context. Add a real preview-process cancellation test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"A nested executeTool call without its own signal inherits cancellation sufficiently to settle a pending approval when the outer call aborts.","evidence":"The executor passes only 'deps.signal' to 'gate().ask(request, deps.signal)'. ApprovalBroker installs its cancellation listener only on that supplied signal; APPROVAL_WAIT_MS is 300000. The design makes currentToolSignal read only by the shell helper and establishes the nested context only around execute. Consequently, a nested destructive call with no deps.signal can remain awaiting approval for five minutes after the outer stream closes, despite inheriting cancellation for any later shell command. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/approval-broker.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Resolve an effective inherited signal before cancellation checks and approval dispatch, and pass it to the broker as well as execution. Test a nested gated call with no inner signal while a separate approval subscription remains open.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed cancellation tests establish the universal tools.call and nested-call cancellation guarantees.","evidence":"The design tests legacy git_diff, a legacy gh export, the auth probe, git_show and a nested subprocess call. It does not exercise registered direct-spawn streaming tools, cancellation of a real subprocess in buildApprovalGate, or a nested call blocked at an approval gate without its own signal. The corresponding code paths bypass the proposed mechanism, so the listed tests could pass while the advertised guarantees fail. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S007/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/shell/exec-detached.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/cloud/aws/logs.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/approval-broker.ts]","action":"Extend the acceptance mapping with direct-spawn registry coverage, real approval-preview cancellation and nested approval cancellation tests. Retain the existing process-tree and bounded-settlement assertions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":3,"med":1,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T16:21:42.595Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
