9786	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-79ccaf208b61fcd4a8712c40179091b0","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:42:05.629Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD covers the five effective foundation criteria and defers production call-site migration to s9/s10.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md states 's7 is read as the foundations only' and lists ac1–ac5 covering hooks, destructive approval failures, cancellation, typed tools and tools.call/reporting. The design addresses each and leaves replacement and deletion to s9/s10. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain the explicit distinction between effective criteria and the older DEF text.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current executor validates schema-bearing inputs before approval, passes deps.signal only to the approval ask, and returns tool-built failures unchanged.","evidence":"executeTool validates input before buildApprovalRequest, calls 'gate().ask(request, deps.signal)', invokes tool.execute without ambient context, and contains 'if (!result.success) return result;'. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Preserve these ordering and failure-preservation rules while adding cancellation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Killing a git_push or git_reset preview subprocess makes buildApprovalGate throw, causing the generic preview to stand.","evidence":"readBranch returns '{ ok: false, failed: res }' for a killed read; git_push converts that into an '(unknown: ...)' preview. git_reset uses currentBranch's undefined fallback and checks 'forceRead.ok'. These paths return preview objects rather than throwing. buildApprovalRequest's generic fallback applies only when the builder actually throws. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/reset.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Describe the actual fallback behavior and rely on the executor's post-preview cancellation check. Correct the preview fixture too: git_push reads 'symbolic-ref --short HEAD', not 'rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD'.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The provenance check and FieldSpec pattern support are additions to capabilities that currently lack them.","evidence":"callTool currently dispatches by tool.id and casts result.data without checking the registered definition. FieldSpec has kind, values, minimum, description and empty; fieldSchema's string branch supplies minLength and description but no pattern. buildInputSchema already compares shared field specifications through JSON.stringify. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Proceed with the proposed additions and preserve the existing shared-field comparison.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"spawnManaged's declared return contract supports both streaming consumers and the required already-aborted no-spawn case.","evidence":"The design declares 'child: ChildProcess' and simultaneously requires 'aborted true and no process'. Existing streaming consumers immediately access child.stdout, child.stderr and child.on; exec-detached is one example. A no-child return cannot satisfy the declared type or safely support that migration without an explicit branch. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/shell/exec-detached.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/k8s/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/test/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/ssh/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/cloud/aws/logs.ts]","action":"Specify a discriminated return union or an optional child, and require every migrated site to handle the no-spawn branch before attaching callbacks. Cover that branch for the streaming consumers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed tools.call handler can use the existing generic stream transport without changing TrustedRpcContext.","evidence":"StreamHandler receives '(params, send, signal, context)' whereas RpcHandler receives params and context only. directDispatch combines transport lifetime signals and aborts the stream controller on cancellation. TrustedRpcContext already supplies connectionIdentity and optional connectionExecution, with no sessionId. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/request-context.ts]","action":"Keep connectionExecution sourced exclusively from trusted context and test through directDispatch as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The narrowed foundation scope and the four git additions respect the recorded Story ownership decisions; the proposed relationships are adequately documented in prose.","evidence":"The plan explicitly assigns config, ls-remote, update-ref and rm to s7 without adding s8 as a dependency, assigns the tracker family to s7, and moves cutover obligations to s9/s10. The LLD describes wrapper-to-original direction, registration ownership, stream call lifetime and approval subscription ownership. These relationships do not require an ERD to resolve material ambiguity; no companion rendering is claimed verified. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/project.ts]","action":"Retain these ownership descriptions. No additional visual is necessary for the relationships examined.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Running hooks after the tool's runWithToolSignal block ensures hooks are outside the signal context, including nested executeTool calls.","evidence":"The existing executor calls withHooks after awaiting tool.execute, and withHooks directly awaits runToolHooks. Under the proposed AsyncLocalStorage semantics, a nested executor entered from an outer tool's execute continuation restores the outer context after its own run block. Its hooks therefore still inherit the outer signal; runWithToolSignal(undefined) explicitly leaves that context unchanged. Hook subprocesses could consequently be cancelled despite the promised exclusion. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/hooks.ts]","action":"Specify an explicit context-clearing operation around hook execution that clears inherited tool context as well. Add a nested executor test whose hook checks currentToolSignal before and after an await and starts work while the outer signal aborts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An opt-in diagnostic seam must cap failure.original itself because executor-owned truncation does not apply to tool-built failures.","evidence":"ghFailureOf currently derives command-exit original only from probe output and preserves stderr in the spawn-error branch. defineGhFamily returns that failure before shaping output. executeTool returns unsuccessful tool results unchanged; its 4000-character truncation is confined to its own failed helper. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Keep the diagnostic cap in ghFailureOf and preserve existing non-opt-in failure objects as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each effective acceptance criterion has a concrete planned proving test using the existing executor and registry test seams.","evidence":"The five criteria in the plan map to workflow hook tests, approval denial tests, cancellation/deadline tests, typing and tool-family tests, and stream/scan tests in the LLD. Existing call-tool.test.ts already exercises registered definitions, schema mismatch, tool failures and unregistered ids; executor.ts exposes the approval-gate seam, and _fakes.ts supplies typed schemas and ToolDeps. These are planned tests, not verified implemented tests. The analyzer was attempted but did not return before termination; findings were grounded through direct source reads. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/call-tool.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/_fakes.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, tsconfig.json]","action":"Retain the acceptance mapping, correct the preview command fixture, and add the no-child and nested-hook cases identified above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":1,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T16:42:05.629Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
