10529	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s7","entry":{"id":"review-d4296cb924b0c4fa937ea5e1483b9c73","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:57:44.866Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the five effective s7 foundation criteria and leaves production call-site migration to s9 and s10.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly says 's7 is read as the foundations only' and enumerates hooks, approval failures, cancellation, typed tools, tools.call and the report-mode scan. The design addresses these and preserves the documented handoff. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain the explicit distinction between effective criteria and the older DEF criteria.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The changed relationships are adequately documented without mandatory companion diagrams.","evidence":"The supplied design identifies executor-to-context ownership, wrapper-to-original provenance direction and cardinality, stream ownership of cancellation, daemon ownership of approvals, and compatibility. These descriptions can be checked against executor.ts, hooks.ts, registry.ts, approval.ts and server.ts. No linked generated visual is claimed or supplied for verification. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/hooks.ts, src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/approval.ts, src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"No additional visual is required for these relationships.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The executor currently validates schema-bearing inputs before approval, passes only deps.signal to approval, executes without a cancellation recheck, and returns tool-built failures unchanged.","evidence":"executeTool validates input before buildApprovalRequest, calls 'gate().ask(request, deps.signal)', then 'await tool.execute(input, deps)' without an abort check, and contains 'if (!result.success) return result;'. Hooks run at the checked-success exits. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Preserve this pipeline order while adding effective-signal handling.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runShell lacks an entry abort check and process-group kill; runShellBytes has both but lacks bounded settlement after killing.","evidence":"runShell spawns immediately and its abort handler calls child.kill('SIGKILL'). runShellBytes checks 'options.signal?.aborted', uses detached processes and process.kill(-child.pid, 'SIGKILL'), but finish is called only from error and close handlers. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Implement the shared bounded lifecycle as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed provenance check fills a real gap and accommodates the existing git and gh wrapper shapes.","evidence":"callTool currently dispatches only by tool.id and casts result.data. registerTool overwrites byId entries. Git registration wraps exported definitions with withFailureNet; ghProjectListTool is exported directly from withGhFailureNet, and defineGhFamily also returns that wrapper. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/project.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Keep identity equality as the first acceptance case and record immediate originals for wrapper chains.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"FieldSpec patterns and the path, kv and qs argument variants are additive capabilities missing from the current op table.","evidence":"FieldSpec currently has kind, values, minimum, description and empty. Arg contains pos, spread, last, flag and lit. buildInputSchema compares shared specifications using JSON.stringify after removing description and values. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Retain string-valued patterns and regression checks for existing argv generation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The paginated tracker operations can obtain their declared complete results merely by parsing the JSON printed by the specified --paginate commands.","evidence":"The proposed comments_list, issues_by_labels and issues_titles argv use '--paginate' without a defined page-framing strategy. Existing listing wrappers instead use '-q', then split output into lines. The reusable parseJson helper performs one JSON.parse(raw), and defineGhFamily forwards the entire captured stdout to the custom builder. Multiple page arrays are not one JSON document, so the specified single-JSON parsing contract does not establish working multi-page results. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Specify an explicit framing strategy for all three operations, such as --slurp with flattening or line-delimited extraction, and update exact argv and multi-page fixtures accordingly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed tools.call stream can use the existing stream dispatch and remain on the main thread under current routing.","evidence":"directDispatch passes params, send, a combined abort signal and trusted context to stream handlers. Router dispatches locally when a class is not in routed. Daemon startup adds indexing and admin to routed; session methods remain local. TrustedRpcContext supplies connectionIdentity and has no sessionId. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/request-context.ts, src/daemon/threads/router.ts, src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"Add the handler and method-class entry as proposed; preserve trusted-context-only execution metadata.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The examined foundation changes require no persisted-record migration.","evidence":"The registry is an in-memory Map, hook registration is an in-memory Map, and callTool operates on runtime definitions and ToolResult. The proposed WeakMap provenance and async signal context do not alter persisted entities. The examined gh schema and argument additions preserve existing specifications by default. [files: src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/hooks.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Keep the new timeout, pattern and diagnostic options additive; preserve existing failure objects for operations that do not opt in.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Building the tracker family and four additional git commands in s7 follows the recorded scope amendments rather than taking unapproved adjacent-story work.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md records the user's decisions that 's7 builds the narrow typed tracker family' and 's7 builds config, ls-remote, update-ref and rm', without adding s8 to dependsOn. Its split section assigns site moves and deletion to s9 and s10. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Keep production wrapper replacement and shared-deadline creation in the later stories.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The opt-in diagnostic seam must cap command-exit diagnostics itself because the executor does not cap tool-built failures.","evidence":"ghFailureOf currently derives command-exit original from probe text and preserves stderr for spawn errors. executeTool returns unsuccessful tool results unchanged; only its own failed helper slices original to 4000 characters. The proposed seam correctly identifies where the new cap must apply. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Implement the cap at ghFailureOf's opted-in command-exit branches and retain the spawn-error behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The effective acceptance criteria have concrete planned tests, including the high-risk cancellation, typing and registry paths.","evidence":"Compared with the five effective criteria in tool-registry.md, the supplied acceptance mapping covers workflow hooks and approval, shared cancellation, typed tool contracts, tools.call validation and the scan. Existing shell-helper behavior and tsconfig exclusions substantiate the need for process-tree tests and a separate noEmit type-check configuration. These are planned tests, not executed implementation evidence. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, tsconfig.json]","action":"Retain the mapping and ensure paginated tracker fixtures exercise actual multi-page CLI framing, addressing the change-sites finding.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T16:57:44.866Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
